# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
C('paraplu', "one adult in plain clothes stands whole-figure, front view, in a plain doorway, a plain umbrella with a curved handle, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall beside the door. Only whether the adult holds the umbrella or it stands in a stand behind them changes.",
  "Ik neem mijn paraplu mee, maar mijn broer laat zijn paraplu thuis achter.", "I take my umbrella with me, but my brother leaves his umbrella at home.")
K('meenemen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult steps out of the open front door towards the viewer and holds a closed umbrella in one hand by the curved handle, the other hand on the door; a small arrow points out of the doorway towards the viewer. The umbrella stand beside the door is empty.",
  "an umbrella in the adult's hand at the door beside an empty stand.",
  "the umbrella left standing in the stand as the adult leaves (achterlaten); an adult carrying a heavy box (optillen); an adult opening an umbrella in rain (not the card); an adult holding hands with a child (not the card).",
  "Pair with achterlaten. The only difference is where the umbrella is: in the adult's hand here, standing in the stand there.",
  "neem ... mee", "Ik neem mijn paraplu mee.", "I take my umbrella with me.", "heeft meegenomen",
  "Een volwassene staat bij de open voordeur met een paraplu in de hand en de paraplubak naast de deur is leeg.")
K('achterlaten', "One drawing, one panel. An adult steps out of the open front door towards the viewer, hands empty and swinging, while a plain umbrella stays standing in the umbrella stand beside the door behind them. A small arrow points out of the doorway towards the viewer.",
  "an umbrella standing in the stand as the empty-handed adult walks out.",
  "the adult holding the umbrella in the doorway (meenemen); an umbrella dropped on a street (not the card); an adult hiding an umbrella in a cupboard (not the card); a locked door with nobody near it (afsluiten).",
  "Pair with meenemen. The only difference is the umbrella: in the stand with an empty-handed adult here, in the adult's hand there.",
  "laat ... achter", "Ik laat mijn paraplu thuis achter.", "I leave my umbrella at home.", "heeft achtergelaten",
  "Een volwassene loopt met lege handen de voordeur uit terwijl een paraplu in de bak blijft staan.")

C('kamer', "one plain room seen from the front with a flat floor, a toy box with an open lid on the floor, a plain shelf on the back wall, one adult in plain clothes at the middle, same viewpoint. Only the thing being done changes: a toy dropping into the box, or a cloth wiping the floor.",
  "Ik ruim mijn kamer op en daarna maak ik de vloer schoon.", "I tidy my room and then I clean the floor.")
K('opruimen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult bends over the open toy box and lets a toy drop from one hand into it, a short downward arrow under the toy. The box is half full and two toys still lie on the floor beside the adult's feet.",
  "a toy dropping into a half-full box with two toys still on the floor.",
  "the same room with the floor being wiped with a cloth (schoonmaken); an adult throwing toys in a bin (weggooien); an adult counting toys on a shelf (not the card); an adult sweeping crumbs from a table (not the card).",
  "Pair with schoonmaken. The only difference is the hands: a toy dropping into the box here, a cloth wiping the floor there.",
  "ruim ... op", "Ik ruim mijn kamer op.", "I tidy my room.", "heeft opgeruimd",
  "Een volwassene laat een speelgoedje in een halfvolle kist vallen en er liggen nog twee speelgoedjes op de vloer.")
K('schoonmaken', "One drawing, one panel. An adult kneels beside a bucket and wipes the floor with a cloth moving to one side. Ahead of the cloth lie small dirt flecks; behind it the floor is bare with three sparkle lines. The toy box stands shut in the background.",
  "a cloth with dirt flecks ahead of it and sparkle lines behind it.",
  "the same room with toys going into the box (opruimen); an adult washing dishes (afwassen); an adult sweeping with a broom and no cloth (not the card); an adult spraying a window (not the card).",
  "Pair with opruimen. The only difference is the hands: a cloth wiping the floor here, a toy dropping into the box there.",
  "maak ... schoon", "Ik maak de vloer schoon.", "I clean the floor.", "heeft schoongemaakt",
  "Een volwassene boent met een doek over de vloer: voor de doek liggen vlekjes, achter de doek glanst de vloer.")

C('jas', "one adult in plain clothes stands whole-figure, front view, beside a plain wall hook and a plain coat, same distance from the viewer, a flat floor line and a plain wall behind. Only whether the coat is on the adult's body or in the adult's hands changes.",
  "Ik trek mijn jas aan en thuis trek ik hem weer uit.", "I put on my coat and at home I take it off again.")
K('aantrekken', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands facing the viewer with one arm through a coat sleeve while the coat rises onto the second shoulder and the second arm slides into its sleeve, a small arrow pointing up beside the coat, the empty wall hook beside them.",
  "a coat rising onto the second shoulder with an upward arrow.",
  "the coat being pulled off over the shoulders (uittrekken); an adult holding a coat on a hanger (not the card); an adult tying a scarf (not the card); an adult pulling a rope (not the card).",
  "Pair with uittrekken. The only difference is the coat: rising onto the shoulders with an arrow up here, down at the elbows with an arrow down there.",
  "trek ... aan", "Ik trek mijn jas aan.", "I put on my coat.", "heeft aangetrokken",
  "Een volwassene steekt de armen in de mouwen en de jas schuift omhoog over de schouders.")
K('uittrekken', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands facing the viewer with the coat pulled down off both shoulders to the elbows, both arms still in the sleeves, a small arrow pointing down beside the coat, the empty wall hook beside them.",
  "a coat down at the elbows with a downward arrow.",
  "the coat going on with one sleeve empty (aantrekken); an adult hanging a coat on the hook (not the card); a coat lying on the floor (not the card); an adult pulling a tooth (not the card).",
  "Pair with aantrekken. The only difference is the coat: down at the elbows with an arrow down here, rising onto the shoulders with an arrow up there.",
  "trek ... uit", "Ik trek mijn jas uit.", "I take off my coat.", "heeft uitgetrokken",
  "Een volwassene laat een jas van beide schouders tot de ellebogen zakken.")

C('bed', "one plain single bed seen side-on with a pillow and a blanket, a bedside table with a blank-faced alarm clock, no numerals, a window behind, same distance from the viewer. Only whether the sleeper is rising off the bed at first light or still lying in it with the sun high changes.",
  "Op werkdagen sta ik vroeg op, maar op zondag slaap ik uit.", "On workdays I get up early, but on Sunday I sleep in.")
K('opstaan', "One drawing, one panel. An adult rises off the edge of the bed, weight on both feet, knees straightening and hips lifted clear of the mattress, the blanket pushed back; the blank-faced alarm clock has two short ring lines and a low sun sits at the bottom of the window.",
  "an adult rising off the mattress onto both feet with the alarm ringing.",
  "an adult lying asleep in the bed with a blanket up to the chin (uitslapen); an adult sitting in a chair at a table (not the card); an adult standing up from a chair (not the card); an adult jumping on the bed (not the card).",
  "Pair with uitslapen. The only difference is the sleeper: rising onto the feet with a ringing clock and low sun here, lying still with a silent clock and high sun there.",
  "sta ... op", "Ik sta om zeven uur op.", "I get up at seven o'clock.", "is opgestaan",
  "Een volwassene komt van het bed overeind op beide voeten en naast het bed rinkelt een wekker.")
K('uitslapen', "One drawing, one panel. The same adult lies in the bed on one side with eyes closed and a content small smile, the blanket up to the chin; the blank-faced alarm clock is silent with no ring lines, and the sun stands high in the window with long rays.",
  "a sleeper in bed under a high sun with a silent clock.",
  "an adult sitting on the bed edge with a ringing clock (opstaan); an adult napping in an armchair (not the card); an adult lying awake with open eyes (not the card); a child jumping on the bed (not the card).",
  "Pair with opstaan. The only difference is the sleeper: lying still under a high sun with a silent clock here, rising onto the feet with a ringing clock there.",
  "slaap ... uit", "Op zondag slaap ik uit.", "On Sunday I sleep in.", "heeft uitgeslapen",
  "Een volwassene ligt met gesloten ogen onder een deken, de zon is hoog en de wekker is stil.")

C('bestelbus', "one plain delivery van seen side-on with its rear doors open, a flat road line, three plain cardboard boxes of the same size, same distance from the viewer, one adult in plain clothes at the open rear doors. Only whether the boxes go into the van or come out of it changes.",
  "Eerst laad ik de dozen in en bij de winkel laad ik ze uit.", "First I load the boxes in and at the shop I unload them.")
K('inladen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands at the open back of a plain van lifting a box up onto the van floor, two boxes already stacked inside and one box still on the road beside the adult's feet, a small arrow pointing into the van.",
  "a box being lifted up into the van with others already stacked inside.",
  "boxes being carried out of the van onto the road (uitladen); an adult driving the van (not the card); an adult packing a suitcase (inpakken); an adult lifting one heavy box on an empty road (optillen).",
  "Pair with uitladen. The only difference is the direction: boxes going up into the van here, down onto the road there.",
  "laad ... in", "Ik laad de dozen in.", "I load the boxes.", "heeft ingeladen",
  "Een volwassene schuift een doos in de achterkant van een bestelbus waar al twee dozen staan.")
K('uitladen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands at the open back of the same van lifting a box down from the van floor onto the road, two boxes already stacked on the road and one box still inside, a small arrow pointing out of the van.",
  "a box being lowered from the van onto the road beside a stack on the ground.",
  "boxes being lifted into the van (inladen); an adult unpacking clothes from a suitcase (uitpakken); a van parked with the doors shut (not the action); an adult pushing a trolley (not the card).",
  "Pair with inladen. The only difference is the direction: boxes going down onto the road here, up into the van there.",
  "laad ... uit", "Ik laad de dozen bij de winkel uit.", "I unload the boxes at the shop.", "heeft uitgeladen",
  "Een volwassene haalt een doos uit de achterkant van een bestelbus en op de weg staan al twee dozen.")

C('vliegtuig', "one plain passenger plane seen side-on over a long flat runway line with a plain control-tower box at the far end, same size on the page, a plain sky behind. Only whether the plane is rising from the runway changes; the set has no drawn partner.",
  "Het vliegtuig stijgt om negen uur op.", "The plane takes off at nine o'clock.")
K('opstijgen', "SKIP: no separable opposite. landen is not separable and already has its card in Werkwoorden (a1-regular, landen), and neerkomen reads as a crash, so a one-verb set cannot show the contrast.",
  "-", "-", "-", "stijgt ... op", "Het vliegtuig stijgt op.", "The plane takes off.", "is opgestegen", "-")
